used to train the machine learning models.

The authors also acknowledge the use of the following open-source libraries
and tools: scikit-learn, OpenCV, Flask, Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, Seaborn,
Pillow, and the Railway platform for deployment.

Authors' contributions:
A.D. conducted the literature review on neuromarketing and visual persuasion,
designed the five evaluation dimensions, and wrote the project documentation.
L.Z. set up the GitHub repository and managed the deployment on Railway.
A.D. and L.Z. jointly developed the full Python pipeline (data preparation,
model training, analysis, and web interface) and collaborated on debugging
and testing throughout the development process.
